# Sheet Pan Chicken and Veg (Freezer to Oven)

Makes 6 servings per pan (4 for dinner, 1 for a snack, 1 for a next-day lunch) — prep 2-3 pans/bags on the weekend.

## Ingredients
- 6 boneless chicken thighs
- 1 1/2 lb baby potatoes, halved
- 3 cups broccoli florets or mixed vegetables
- 4 tbsp olive oil
- 1 1/2 tsp garlic powder
- 1 1/2 tsp paprika
- Salt and pepper to taste

## Instructions
1. Toss chicken, potatoes, and vegetables with olive oil and seasonings.
2. Spread on a sheet pan lined with parchment, or pack flat into a gallon freezer bag.
3. Freeze flat (bag) or wrap tightly (pan) for up to 3 months.
4. On cook night: bake at 400°F for 35-40 minutes if thawed, or 45-55 minutes straight from frozen, until chicken reaches 165°F.

## Notes
- One pan, one cleanup — no extra pots or knife work needed on the night you cook it.
- Swap in whatever vegetables hold up well to roasting: carrots, green beans, bell peppers.
- Set aside the extra 2 pieces before serving — one for a snack, one packed for the next day's lunch.
